\paragraph{E.1 SP2-05 Historical Reconstruction}\label{app:sp205}
\label{sec:s-sp205}
The historical population contains 74 sessions: 161 model-turn, 106 run, and 74 session-end events, including 42 oracle successes, two oracle failures, and 30 no-verdict sessions. The V2/V3 result trees are byte-identical copies of these sessions, giving 74 observations rather than 148. Transcript hashes identify 35 exact migrated
duplicates and 39 raw-only sessions. Admissibility tiers are A=35, B=25,
C=14, D=0. No exact runtime revision is recoverable for every session;
literal raw prompts are incomplete, model labels mutable, and born-valid
identity linkage incomplete. Different tasks, schema, prompt retention,
oracle/source pins, and status lineage prevent pooling with the 54-row E2.
The 35 migrated and 39 raw-only sessions partition that retained population; neither directory copies nor migration add executions.
